//! Fitted SDTM-1 solar-wind field -- generated by `tools/fit-sdtm-corpus.py`, do not edit.
//!
//! Fitted 2026-10-30 by `tools/fit-sdtm-corpus.py` on 365214 rows,
//! every 60th of the TU Delft v02 corpus (`docs/verification.md` §10.20):
//! CHAMP, GRACE A/B, GOCE, GRACE-FO C and Swarm A/B/C, 2000-07 to 2026-04, from TU Delft,
//! Siemes et al. (2023), CC BY 4.0 -- which is the attribution that licence asks of adapted
//! material, and `docs/provenance.md` (`sdtm-reference`) is the rest of it.
//!
//! Degree 2, harmonic caps `storm-log1-lin`: 36 of the 144 possible
//! coefficients, ridge 0.001, the Bates shape fitted, the boundary scale fitted (on its bound).
//! The storm driver is heating with nitric-oxide cooling (`derivations/sdtm_no_cooling.mac`).
//! It runs hourly on (1 - s) ap60 + s N, s = 0.500 fitted (`DRIVE`): GFZ's ap60, and N
//! Newell et al. (2007)'s coupling of NASA's OMNI solar wind on ap60's scale, by a table whose
//! 34 knots are read off the 241531 hours both series have, 1999-01-01T00 to
//! 2026-09-13T23: OMNI from NASA/GSFC's SPDF, CC0 1.0 (King & Papitashvili 2005,
//! doi:10.1029/2004JA010649), and ap60 from GFZ Helmholtz Centre for Geosciences, CC BY 4.0
//! (Matzka et al. 2024, doi:10.5880/Hpo.0003), which is the attribution that licence asks of
//! adapted material. An hour without the solar wind takes its ap60.
//! The daily flux excess saturates as D tanh(d/D), D fitted (`derivations/sdtm_flux_excess.mac`).
//! The storm driver scales as (F10.7a/150)^kappa, kappa fitted (`derivations/sdtm_storm_gain.mac`).
//! Held out by mission family, MAPE 20.5 % pooled.
//!
//! The uncertainty table below is that held-out residual's spread about zero, per regime. A
//! table built without one family's rows has a 90 % interval that covers, of that family:
//! CHAMP 92.7 %,
//! GOCE 99.6 %,
//! GRACE 87.1 %,
//! GRACE-FO 88.1 %,
//! Swarm 92.0 %,
//!
//! The fit's own verdict, the folds it was scored on and what it does not claim are in
//! `docs/verification.md` §10.21-§10.32.
